 @viclee4346  I tried purchasing their policy on the 23rd of February. Until then, their so-called "CRM" was in constant contact with me. However, once I made the payment, I was redirected to an error screen. At first, I thought it was a bank server issue—but it wasn’t.

I reached out to the CRM for help in resolving the issue, but he was of no help at all. I even requested to be connected to a senior Customer Relationship Manager, but he refused. To get my money refunded, the bank required an email from Niva Bupa stating that they hadn't received the payment. When I asked the CRM if he could provide such an email, he again said no.

Finally, I mentioned that I might need to approach the Consumer Court, to which he responded, "Do whatever you feel is right"—and washed his hands off the issue entirely.

